        <section id="overview" class="api-doc-section api-doc-hero">
            <p class="api-doc-kicker">Edge AI Client API</p>
            <h1>SentriBee Console API Documentation</h1>
            <p>
                These APIs connect Edge AI programs to SentriBee Console. Clients authenticate with a project API key,
                exchange it for a short-lived bearer token, report runtime health every 30 seconds, and upload detected
                events for server-side workflow processing.
            </p>
            <div class="api-doc-meta">
                <span>Base URL</span>
                <code>https://console.sentribee.ai</code>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="security" class="api-doc-section">
            <h2>Security Model</h2>
            <p>
                Project API keys are generated in Project Settings. The full key is displayed only once and the server
                stores only a SHA-256 hash. Edge clients should call the authentication endpoint during startup, cache
                the returned bearer token in memory, and refresh it before expiry.
            </p>
            <div class="api-doc-callout">
                Use the long-lived project API key only for token exchange. All normal telemetry and event requests
                should use <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;accessToken&gt;</code>.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="app-client" class="api-doc-section">
            <h2>App Client API</h2>
            <p>
                Client apps first use the common project authentication endpoint <code>/api/edge/auth</code>. The returned
                project bearer token is required for email verification, registration, and login. Registration and login then return
                an app bearer token for QR binding and device queries.
            </p>
            <table class="api-doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Auth</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>POST /api/app/auth/email-code</code></td><td>Send an Amazon SES email verification code.</td><td>Project Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>POST /api/app/auth/register</code></td><td>Create a new email user, collect phone device info, and return a 30-day app token.</td><td>Project Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>POST /api/app/auth/login</code></td><td>Login an existing email user, update phone device/push info, and return a 30-day app token.</td><td>Project Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/profile</code></td><td>Return the current logged-in app user's profile.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>PUT /api/app/profile</code></td><td>Update display name, first name, last name, and gender for the current app user.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>POST /api/app/devices/bind</code></td><td>Bind the logged-in user to a permanent short Edge Device QR code.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/devices</code></td><td>List all Edge Devices bound to the current app user.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/devices/running</code></td><td>Compatibility alias for all bound devices.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}</code></td><td>Return stream URL, today's people/equipment counts, cameras, and the current user's risk push settings for a bound device.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}/daily-stats</code></td><td>Return historical daily people, bracelet, vehicle, PPE, and risk statistics.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}/risk-subjects</code></td><td>Return the people with the most risk reports for a selected day.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}/risk-notification-settings</code></td><td>Return per-place risk push settings for the current app user.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>PUT /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}/risk-notification-settings</code></td><td>Update which verified risk levels should trigger app push for this place.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/notifications</code></td><td>Return unread or recent verified-risk notification records.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>PUT /api/app/notifications/{notificationId}/read</code></td><td>Mark one notification as read.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/events/{eventId}/analysis</code></td><td>Return event-level people, vehicle, PPE, and per-person crop analysis.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/events/{eventId}/image</code></td><td>Stream a bound event image through the server for private S3 objects.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>GET /api/app/edge-event-subjects/{subjectId}/image/{kind}</code></td><td>Stream a risk-person crop or preview through the server for private S3 objects.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>DELETE /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}/binding</code></td><td>Remove the current app user's binding from an Edge Device.</td><td>App Bearer</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <h3>Register Flow</h3>
            <p>
                If a new email asks for a code with <code>purpose</code> set to <code>Login</code> or omitted, Console stores it as a
                registration code. Existing registered emails receive login codes. This allows a single mobile email-code screen
                to support both new and existing users.
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>POST /api/app/auth/email-code
Authorization: Bearer sb_token_...
{
  "email": "site.manager@example.com",
  "purpose": "Register"
}

POST /api/app/auth/register
Authorization: Bearer sb_token_...
{
  "email": "site.manager@example.com",
  "verificationCode": "123456",
  "displayName": "Site Manager",
  "firstName": "Site",
  "lastName": "Manager",
  "gender": "Prefer not to say",
  "device": {
    "deviceIdentifier": "ios-vendor-id-or-android-id",
    "deviceType": "iPhone 15 Pro",
    "platform": "iOS",
    "osVersion": "18.5",
    "appVersion": "1.0.0",
    "pushProvider": "apns",
    "pushToken": "push-token-for-future-notifications"
  }
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Login Flow</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>POST /api/app/auth/email-code
Authorization: Bearer sb_token_...
{
  "email": "site.manager@example.com",
  "purpose": "Login"
}

POST /api/app/auth/login
Authorization: Bearer sb_token_...
{
  "email": "site.manager@example.com",
  "verificationCode": "123456",
  "device": {
    "deviceIdentifier": "ios-vendor-id-or-android-id",
    "deviceType": "iPhone 15 Pro",
    "platform": "iOS",
    "osVersion": "18.5",
    "appVersion": "1.0.0",
    "pushProvider": "apns",
    "pushToken": "push-token-for-future-notifications"
  }
}</code></pre>
            <h3>App Profile</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>GET /api/app/profile
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...

PUT /api/app/profile
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...
{
  "displayName": "Site Manager",
  "firstName": "Site",
  "lastName": "Manager",
  "gender": "Female"
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Email Delivery</h3>
            <p>
                Email verification uses Amazon SES v2. Configure <code>EmailAuth__FromAddress</code> and
                <code>EmailAuth__SesRegion</code>. When SES-specific access keys are not supplied, Console reuses
                <code>S3Storage__AccessKeyId</code> and <code>S3Storage__SecretAccessKey</code> for SES signing. The AWS
                identity must allow <code>ses:SendEmail</code> for the verified SES identity used as the from address.
            </p>
            <h3>Bind Device</h3>
            <p>
                The Edge Device QR image contains only the permanent short binding code, for example <code>SB8F3K2Q9</code>.
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>POST /api/app/devices/bind
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...
{
  "bindingCode": "SB8F3K2Q9"
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Bound Device List</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>GET /api/app/devices
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...

DELETE /api/app/devices/EDGE-20260528-53A1688A4/binding
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...</code></pre>
            <h3>Daily Stats and Risk People</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>GET /api/app/devices/EDGE-20260528-53A1688A4/daily-stats?from=2026-06-01&amp;to=2026-06-30
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...

GET /api/app/devices/EDGE-20260528-53A1688A4/risk-subjects?date=2026-06-02
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...

GET /api/app/events/1842/analysis
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...</code></pre>
            <p>
                Person crop URLs returned by risk-subject and event-analysis endpoints are server proxy URLs, not raw S3 URLs.
                Use the same app bearer token when loading those images so private S3 bucket permissions do not leak to the app.
            </p>
            <p>
                Device detail uses today's daily stat row for <code>recognizableWorkerCount</code>,
                <code>heavyEquipmentCount</code>, and <code>ppeComplianceRate</code>. If today's row is not available yet,
                Console falls back to the latest heartbeat detail metrics. <code>cameraCount</code> is counted from camera/RTSP
                endpoints configured under that Edge Device.
            </p>
            <h3>Risk Notification Settings</h3>
            <p>
                Settings are stored per app user and per bound place. Defaults are <code>Severe Danger</code> enabled,
                <code>Ordinary Risk</code> disabled, and legacy <code>Real Risk</code> disabled. The app can update them at any time.
                The same setting list is also included in <code>GET /api/app/devices/{deviceCode}</code> as
                <code>riskNotificationSettings</code> so the detail screen can render and save the toggles without a separate
                initial fetch.
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>GET /api/app/devices/EDGE-20260528-53A1688A4/risk-notification-settings
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...

PUT /api/app/devices/EDGE-20260528-53A1688A4/risk-notification-settings
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...
{
  "severeDangerEnabled": true,
  "ordinaryRiskEnabled": false,
  "realRiskEnabled": false
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Unread Risk Notifications</h3>
            <p>
                When an event is verified as a real risk, Console creates one unread notification for each app user bound to that
                place. If the user's risk setting allows that severity, <code>pushStatus</code> is <code>Queued</code>; otherwise it is
                <code>Suppressed</code>. When APNS is configured, queued iOS notifications are sent immediately and the record moves
                to <code>Delivered</code> or <code>Failed</code> with the APNS id or error stored for diagnostics.
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>GET /api/app/notifications?unreadOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...

PUT /api/app/notifications/9001/read
Authorization: Bearer sb_app_...</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="authentication" class="api-doc-section">
            <div class="api-doc-endpoint-heading">
                <div>
                    <h2>Authentication</h2>
                    <p>Exchange a project API key for a bearer token.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="api-endpoint"><span>POST</span><code>/api/edge/auth</code></div>
            </div>
            <h3>Request Body</h3>
            <table class="api-doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>apiKey</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Project API key generated in Project Settings.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>clientName</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Readable client name for audit and troubleshooting.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="api-doc-grid">
                <div>
                    <h3>Example Request</h3>
                    <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "apiKey": "sb_live_...",
  "clientName": "edge-ai-west-gate-01"
}</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Example Response</h3>
                    <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "accessToken": "sb_token_...",
  "tokenType": "Bearer",
  "expiresAtUtc": "2026-05-29T14:30:00Z",
  "projectId": 1,
  "projectName": "PREVENX Edge AI"
}</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="heartbeat" class="api-doc-section">
            <div class="api-doc-endpoint-heading">
                <div>
                    <h2>Heartbeat</h2>
                    <p>Report Edge AI runtime and device connection health every 30 seconds.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="api-endpoint"><span>POST</span><code>/api/edge/heartbeat</code></div>
            </div>
            <h3>Headers</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;accessToken&gt;
Content-Type: application/json</code></pre>
            <h3>Request Body</h3>
            <table class="api-doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>deviceCode</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Existing Edge Device code in the same project.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>runtimeStatus</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Program status, such as <code>Running</code>, <code>Degraded</code>, or <code>Stopped</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>deviceStatus</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Device connectivity, such as <code>Online</code> or <code>Offline</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>reportedAtUtc</code></td><td>datetime</td><td>No</td><td>Client-side report time. Server UTC time is used when omitted.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>peopleCount</code></td><td>number</td><td>No</td><td>Current people count in the scene.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>braceletCount</code></td><td>number</td><td>No</td><td>Current detected Bluetooth safety bracelet count.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>machineryVehicleCount</code></td><td>number</td><td>No</td><td>Current machinery or heavy vehicle count in the scene.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>detailJson</code></td><td>object</td><td>No</td><td>Additional runtime details such as camera count, model version, CPU, memory, or queue depth. Risk counts and verified PPE rates are produced from event review, not heartbeat.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <h3>Example</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "deviceCode": "EDGE-20260529-7A12B4",
  "runtimeStatus": "Running",
  "deviceStatus": "Online",
  "reportedAtUtc": "2026-05-29T02:30:00Z",
  "peopleCount": 12,
  "braceletCount": 10,
  "machineryVehicleCount": 2,
  "detailJson": {
    "cameraConnected": true,
    "modelVersion": "yolo-v8-site-safety-1.4",
    "fps": 18.7
  }
}</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="events" class="api-doc-section">
            <div class="api-doc-endpoint-heading">
                <div>
                    <h2>Event Upload</h2>
                    <p>Submit events detected by Edge AI for server-side rules, notification, review, and training workflows.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="api-endpoint"><span>POST</span><code>/api/edge/events</code></div>
            </div>
            <h3>Request Body</h3>
            <table class="api-doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>deviceCode</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Existing Edge Device code in the same project.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>title</code></td><td>string</td><td>Yes</td><td>Short event name shown in Console event lists.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Human-readable context or detection summary.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>eventTimeUtc</code></td><td>datetime</td><td>No</td><td>Detection time. Server UTC time is used when omitted.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>imageUrl</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Existing image URL when the client already uploaded the image.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>imageBase64</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Base64 image content. The server uploads it to the <code>sentribeebus</code> S3 bucket.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>imageContentType</code></td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td><code>image/jpeg</code> by default; <code>image/png</code> is also supported.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>detectionJson</code></td><td>object</td><td>No</td><td>Detection metadata such as labels, confidence, bounding boxes, and model version.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>analysis</code></td><td>object</td><td>No</td><td>Event-level counts and risk summary. The server verifies PPE risk first, then stores statistics from the verified result.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>subjects</code></td><td>array</td><td>No</td><td>Per-person or per-object boxes, crop URLs, PPE boxes, and risk details.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <h3>Example</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "deviceCode": "EDGE-20260529-7A12B4",
  "title": "PPE violation",
  "description": "Helmet missing near entry zone",
  "eventTimeUtc": "2026-05-29T02:31:00Z",
  "imageBase64": "...",
  "imageContentType": "image/jpeg",
  "detectionJson": {
    "class": "missing_helmet",
    "confidence": 0.93,
    "box": { "x": 220, "y": 88, "w": 140, "h": 240 }
  },
  "analysis": {
    "peopleCount": 3,
    "machineryVehicleCount": 1,
    "toolCount": 2,
    "ppeCompliantPeopleCount": 2,
    "riskPersonCount": 1,
    "ppeComplianceRate": 66.7,
    "riskCategory": "PPE helmet risk",
    "riskSeverity": "Real Risk",
    "summary": "One worker is missing helmet near machinery."
  },
  "subjects": [
    {
      "subjectKey": "person-001",
      "subjectType": "Person",
      "trackingLabel": "Worker 1",
      "cropImageUrl": "https://.../person-001.jpg",
      "previewImageUrl": "https://.../person-001-preview.jpg",
      "boundingBoxJson": { "x": 220, "y": 88, "w": 140, "h": 240 },
      "ppeBoxJson": [{ "class": "vest", "x": 230, "y": 120, "w": 110, "h": 140 }],
      "ppeStatusJson": { "helmet": "missing", "vest": "ok" },
      "isRisk": true,
      "riskCategory": "PPE helmet risk",
      "riskSeverity": "Real Risk",
      "riskReason": "Helmet was not detected on this person."
    }
  ]
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Response</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "success": true,
  "eventId": 1842,
  "imageUrl": "https://sentribeebus.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/edge-events/...",
  "verifiedStatus": "Real Risk",
  "analysis": { "peopleCount": 3, "riskPersonCount": 1, "riskSeverity": "Real Risk" }
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Update Event Analysis</h3>
            <p>
                The ins1 annotation worker can update or replace event analysis after it relabels broad people,
                vehicle, tool, building-material, and large-equipment boxes. Store scene-level boxes in
                <code>analysisJson.panoramaAnnotation</code>, then send each person slice and per-person PPE boxes in
                <code>subjects</code>.
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>POST /api/edge/events/1842/analysis
Authorization: Bearer sb_token_...
{
  "peopleCount": 3,
  "machineryVehicleCount": 1,
  "toolCount": 2,
  "ppeCompliantPeopleCount": 2,
  "riskPersonCount": 1,
  "ppeComplianceRate": 66.7,
  "riskCategory": "PPE helmet risk",
  "riskSeverity": "Real Risk",
  "summary": "One worker is missing helmet.",
  "analysisJson": {
    "model": "ins1-auto-annotation",
    "version": "2026-06-02",
    "panoramaAnnotation": {
      "classes": [
        { "id": 0, "name": "person" },
        { "id": 1, "name": "vehicle" },
        { "id": 2, "name": "tool" },
        { "id": 3, "name": "building_material" }
      ],
      "boxes": [
        { "classId": 0, "x": 220, "y": 88, "w": 140, "h": 240 },
        { "classId": 1, "x": 620, "y": 50, "w": 260, "h": 310 }
      ]
    }
  },
  "subjects": [
    {
      "subjectKey": "person-001",
      "subjectType": "Person",
      "cropImageUrl": "https://.../person-001.jpg",
      "boundingBoxJson": { "x": 220, "y": 88, "w": 140, "h": 240 },
      "ppeBoxJson": [{ "class": "helmet", "status": "missing" }],
      "isRisk": true
    }
  ]
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Remote Auto Analysis Service</h3>
            <p>
                Console can offload event image analysis to the GPU service on <code>ins1.sentribee.ai</code>.
                Set <code>EdgeEventAutoAnalysis:Mode</code> to <code>Remote</code>, configure
                <code>RemoteBaseUrl</code> and <code>RemoteApiKey</code>, then Console will call the internal
                service and save the returned analysis to the database.
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>POST /api/edge-event-analysis/analyze
Authorization: Bearer &lt;RemoteApiKey&gt;
{
  "eventId": 1842,
  "projectId": 1,
  "deviceCode": "EDGE-20260529-7A12B4",
  "imageUrl": "https://sentribeebus.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/edge-events/...",
  "imageBase64": "...",
  "imageContentType": "image/jpeg",
  "detectionJson": { "class": "missing_helmet", "confidence": 0.93 },
  "requiredPpe": ["helmet", "vest"],
  "personConfidence": 0.35,
  "ppeConfidence": 0.35,
  "sceneObjectConfidence": 0.25
}</code></pre>
            <p>
                The response should match the event analysis shape above. Include <code>panoramaAnnotation</code>
                for scene-level boxes and <code>subjects</code> for person crops, PPE boxes, PPE status, and risk flags.
            </p>
            <h3>Optional Event Video Upload</h3>
            <p>
                After creating the event, clients can attach one video by multipart upload. Uploads are associated by
                <code>eventId</code>; retry failed parts by sending the same <code>partNumber</code> again, then call complete.
            </p>
            <table class="api-doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>1</td><td><code>POST /api/edge/events/{eventId}/video/uploads</code></td><td>Start S3 multipart upload and receive <code>videoUploadId</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2</td><td><code>PUT /api/edge/events/{eventId}/video/uploads/{videoUploadId}/parts/{partNumber}</code></td><td>Upload raw binary bytes for one part. Use 8 MB parts except the final part.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>3</td><td><code>GET /api/edge/events/{eventId}/video/uploads/{videoUploadId}</code></td><td>Resume support: list uploaded part numbers and ETags.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>4</td><td><code>POST /api/edge/events/{eventId}/video/uploads/{videoUploadId}/complete</code></td><td>Complete the video and save its S3 URL.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Cancel</td><td><code>DELETE /api/edge/events/{eventId}/video/uploads/{videoUploadId}</code></td><td>Abort an unfinished S3 multipart upload.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <h3>Start Video Upload Body</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "fileName": "event-1842.mp4",
  "contentType": "video/mp4",
  "fileSizeBytes": 73400320
}</code></pre>
            <h3>Start Video Upload Response</h3>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "success": true,
  "eventId": 1842,
  "videoUploadId": 51,
  "uploadId": "...",
  "key": "edge-events/1/EDGE-.../videos/1842/....mp4",
  "recommendedPartSizeBytes": 8388608
}</code></pre>
            <p>
                Complete can omit a body; the server uses the saved uploaded part list. To override, send:
            </p>
            <pre class="api-code"><code>{
  "parts": [
    { "partNumber": 1, "eTag": "\"...\"" },
    { "partNumber": 2, "eTag": "\"...\"" }
  ]
}</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section id="payloads" class="api-doc-section">
            <h2>Payload Rules</h2>
            <ul class="api-doc-list">
                <li>All dates should be ISO 8601 UTC strings, for example <code>2026-05-29T02:31:00Z</code>.</li>
                <li>Heartbeat clients should report every 30 seconds. Missing heartbeats can be treated as offline by later workflow logic.</li>
                <li>Use <code>imageBase64</code> when the Edge program cannot upload directly to storage. Use <code>imageUrl</code> when storage upload is already handled by the client.</li>
                <li>Do not include API keys in logs. Store project API keys in the Edge device secret store or environment configuration.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="errors" class="api-doc-section">
            <h2>Error Responses</h2>
            <table class="api-doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Typical Cause</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>400</code></td><td>Bad Request</td><td>Required fields are missing or malformed.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td>Unauthorized</td><td>API key or bearer token is missing, invalid, expired, or revoked.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>404</code></td><td>Not Found</td><td>The provided <code>deviceCode</code> does not belong to the authenticated project.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>500</code></td><td>Server Error</td><td>Storage, database, or infrastructure failure. Retry with backoff.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>

        <section id="operations" class="api-doc-section">
            <h2>Operational Notes</h2>
            <p>
                Event image upload requires AWS S3 settings on the server: <code>S3Storage__AccessKeyId</code>,
                <code>S3Storage__SecretAccessKey</code>, <code>S3Storage__Region</code>, and <code>S3Storage__Bucket</code>.
                The default bucket is <code>sentribeebus</code>. If these settings are missing, event creation with
                <code>imageUrl</code> still works, but server-side <code>imageBase64</code> upload will fail.
            </p>
        </section>
        </main>
    </div>
</body>
